# Trivy config-scan exemptions. Each entry needs a reason and, ideally, a
# pointer to the runbook that would remove it.
#
# Format: one check ID per line.

# --- NFS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The media library is exported over NFS without Kerberos. This is a known,
# tracked gap with a documented mitigation plan; it is not something a manifest
# change can fix, because the control is on the TrueNAS side.
# See docs/runbooks/nfs-hardening.md
AVD-KSV-0121

# --- hostPath / privileged in the CSI and monitoring namespaces --------------
# democratic-csi node plugins must mount host paths and run privileged to drive
# the host's iSCSI initiator. node-exporter needs hostPID/hostNetwork. Both are
# confined to namespaces labelled `pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: privileged`
# in infrastructure/namespaces/namespaces.yaml, which is the actual control.
AVD-KSV-0009
AVD-KSV-0023

# --- read-only root filesystem ----------------------------------------------
# Several upstream images (Keycloak, the *arr apps, Plex, Seafile) write to their
# own filesystem at runtime and provide no way to relocate that. Enforcing a
# read-only root would mean forking every image.
AVD-KSV-0014
